 spread, and extinction limits for solid fuels burning in low-velocity forced flows in microgravity. 2) Begin to bridge the gap between the normal gravity NASA-STD-6001 Test #1 method, ground-based microgravity tests, and actual material flammability in microgravity. 3) Provide SoFIE PIs with preliminary data to refine Science Requirements. 4) Practical, realistic (thicker) fuels in typical geometries will be examined, including slabs, cylinders, and spherical sections. The primary variables include: Forced flow velocity (speed and direction); Ambient oxygen concentration (via working volume nitrogen vitiation); Sample geometry (rods, spherical section, slabs, films, and fabric sheets)","sensors_evidenced":["Radiometer","O₂ sensor","CO₂ sensor","CO sensor","Still camera","Anemometer (Air display)","Combustion products analyzer (CSA-CP)","CO₂ monitor (CDM)"],"sensors_basis":"Columns for radiometer gain, calibrated O2/CO2/CO and frames shot; air display; CSA-CP and CDM units are named in Appendix A of the Summary Report (test T1).","psi_url":"https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-25","doi_url":"https://doi.org/10.60555/4qc4-de67","row_count":129,"test_count":129,"materials":["Japan Wax","Nomex","PMMA","SIBAL"],"substances":["Japan Wax","Nomex","PMMA","SIBAL"],"variables_recorded":["Oxygen","Airflow","Flow direction","Outcome","Sample shape","Sample thickness","Sample diameter"],"o2_range":{"min":13.6,"max":22.2},"pressure_kpa_range":null,"outcome_fraction":0.86,"has_1g_reference":false,"scale_class":"glovebox","max_sample_area_cm2":null,"max_sample_length_cm":null,"embedded_notes":[],"anomaly_count":42,"column_coverage":[{"column":"PI","recorded":129,"blank":0},{"column":"Test #","recorded":129,"blank":0},{"column":"Date","recorded":129,"blank":0},{"column":"GMT","recorded":129,"blank":0},{"column":"Sample #","recorded":129,"blank":0},{"column":"Fuel Sample Material","recorded":129,"blank":0},{"column":"Flow restrictor","recorded":129,"blank":0},{"c